# Real-Life Event Privacy Rule

- Keep raw family notes, names, addresses, schools, providers, health details, photos, and dates local by default.
- Convert an event into a minimal brief containing only the play theme, relevant feeling or skill, known facts, and content to avoid.
- Send cloud agents only that sanitized brief. Never upload the raw source note as convenience context.
- Do not invent personal facts, motivations, emotions, diagnoses, or outcomes.
- Use real events for preparation, imaginative practice, connection, or reflection—not surveillance or behavioral scoring.
- Store observations as session-level product feedback such as “requested replay” or “left after first round,” not identity labels.
- Parent review is required before event-derived dialogue, art, or pedagogy reaches the iPad.
- If sensitive data appears in a tracked file or Git history, stop cloud handoff, remove it, rotate affected credentials, and report the exposure.
